Round d1_r5 complete. All changes are in `impl/d1_planner.c` and the record is appended to `strategies/d1_planner.md` (including a reconstruction stub for the missing r4 section — that session updated the impl but never wrote its record).

**What shipped (all adoption, named in the record):** paired-p zmm kernels st8@s4 (d1_bluestein r4) / st3@s4 + st5@s12 (d1_rader) into the shared Stockham core — this fixed the one stage every plan ≥1024 runs at half width; the fused forward-last × kernel × inverse-entry mid pass (stmid, d1_bluestein/d1_rader) for both Rader 65537 and Bluestein 10007/100003, so the conv spectrum is never materialized; and d1_composite's twiddle-free PFA-60 codelet plus a fused interleaved-map PFA chain at L=60.

**Verification:** all 52 graded cells PASS on the scoring node (worst rel L2 1.25e-15 vs tol 1e-12), all chain gates ≥3 decades of margin, odd batches pass, output bitwise repeatable. Same-window interleaved A/B vs the r4 build on a80n0: 128 −38%, 1024 −27%, 4096/10007 −20%, 1021 −19%, 16384 −16%, 65537 −10%, 100003 −9%, and L=60 execute 0.135→0.049 (my worst cell, 3.5x gap now ~1.1x); the only flat cells were the two lane-path batched chains, which have no s=4 stage. Measurements are from the reserved Ice Lake node (r3/r4's stale-squeue-shim workaround; lease released), not wallaby.

Technique: paired-p zmm stages + fused conv mid-pass + PFA-60 lift; best node µs/xform — 60: 0.049 (B=1) / 0.050 (B=512), 128: 0.148/0.217, 1024: 1.62/2.18, 1021: 6.67/7.41, 10007: 125/132, 65537: 967/1255, 100003: 3083/3240; worst rel L2 1.25e-15.
